<title>ITALY: Italy's Snia Fibre cuts net losses in 1996.</title>
<headline>Italy's Snia Fibre cuts net losses in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>TURIN, Italy 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Snia Fibre SpA, the chemical and fibre company that is in the process of merging with Snia BPD SpA, reported a reduced net consolidated loss of 10.1 billion lire for 1996 after a loss of 25.7 billion in 1995.</p>
<p>Annual consolidated sales were 1.01 trillion lire after 1.04 trillion in 1995, while the group's gross operating margin rose to 108.2 billion lire from 96.2 billion. Operating profits increased to 29.4 billion lire from 21.9 billion.</p>
<p>((--Milan Newsroom 329 66129502))</p>
</text>
